<title>UK: Commerzbank sets $250 million two-year bond.</title>
<headline>Commerzbank sets $250 million two-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Commerzbank and PaineWebber.</p>
<p> BORROWER   COMMERZBANK</p>
<p> AMT    $250 MLN	COUPON     6.50	MATURITY    07.MAY.99</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.782   PAY DATE  L-06.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.125     REOFFER    99.782    SPREAD	+12 BP</p>
<p> NOTES	L LONG FIRST COUPON</p>
<p> MOODY	AA2	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA-	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/DE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    GERMAN    HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.125     SELL CONC  1.0	 PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.50 PCT U.S. TREASURY DUE MARCH 1999</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF THE EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
